course: dictionary
lesson: 12142
title: Clipped words and their settings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are cut short, especially in informal speech. «Comp» is a clipped word: it is short for «competition», «complimentary» or «composition». Because one short word can stand for several long ones, you must look at the setting to know which meaning is right.
explain: «Maya entered the drawing comp at school and hoped to win the prize.» Entering and winning a prize tell you that comp means a competition. Now read «The theatre gave us two comps, so we sat in the front row for free.» Free seats show that comps here means free tickets.
explain: Ask yourself: what would this word fit next to? A comp can be entered or won, and comps can be given away for free. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Clipped words are short forms of longer words, such as «comp» for «competition».
fact: «Comp» can mean a competition, especially one with a prize, in Britain and Australia.
fact: «Comp» can mean free tickets or items, as in «comps» at a theatre.
fact: In Britain, «comp» can also be short for «comprehensive school», a state secondary school for all abilities.
fact: The same short word can have several meanings, so the setting tells you which one is meant.
exercise: «Maya entered the drawing comp at her school and hoped to win the prize.» What does comp mean here? | A type of music | A free ticket | *A competition | A school for all abilities
exercise: «The theatre gave us two comps, so we sat in the front row for nothing.» What are the comps? | Money paid for a loss | Stories written by children | Prize contests | *Free tickets
exercise: «Dad said he went to the local comp, a state school for all abilities.» Which meaning fits? | A competition with a prize | Free tickets | A piece of music | *A comprehensive school
test: «Our team cannot wait to enter the football comp next week.» What does comp mean here? | A free ticket for the match | *A competition | A school for all abilities | A small bag
test: «Her workers' comp paid her for the weeks she could not work after the accident.» Which long word does comp stand for? | Compilation | Composition | *Compensation | Competition
exam: In a music class, Ali sees «comp» written next to the song he has written, and the teacher says it is his best comp yet. What does comp most likely mean? | Competition | Complimentary | Compensation | *Composition
